# Build-context exclusions for services/tracking (the compose `build:` context).
#
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so the git-ignored 164 MB `.venv/` here would
# otherwise be uploaded as build context AND copied into the image by `COPY src`'s
# sibling copies — a host-built virtualenv whose absolute paths and (on macOS)
# platform wheels are wrong inside a linux container. The Dockerfile installs
# dependencies itself; nothing from the host venv belongs in the image.
#
# The caches below are excluded for the same reason plus layer-cache stability:
# a __pycache__ or .ruff_cache touched by a local test run changes the context
# digest and needlessly invalidates the COPY layer.

# Host virtualenv — never copied, always rebuilt by pip in the builder stage.
.venv/

# Python / tool caches.
# NOTE the `**/` prefixes. Docker's ignore syntax is NOT .gitignore's: a bare
# `__pycache__/` matches only at the CONTEXT ROOT, so without `**/` every nested
# src/**/__pycache__ was copied in — verified, 47 host .pyc files landed in the
# image, compiled as cpython-313 by the host's Python 3.13 and therefore not even
# loadable by this 3.12 runtime.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Not needed to build or run the image
tests/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Local env files are supplied by compose `env_file:` at RUN time ([[env-files]]),
# never baked into the image.
.env
.env.*
